\n[PolarsObjectStore]: got error: Operation not supported: Range request not supported by , will rebuild store and retry\n[dns_cache] ttl: 5s\n[InFlightConcurrency]: observed first RTT sample: 2 ms, for 0 bytes\n```\n\n### Issue description\n\nWith Polars 1.42.1, read_parquet fails to read small parquet files over HTTP with miniserve, where large ones succeed, because of an `object-store` error. Its requested byte range covers the entire file and the server returns the complete representation with 200 OK, which `object-store` doesn't seem to handle gracefully. The same server returns 206 Partial Content for a true subrange of a larger file, which Polars reads successfully.\n\nI'm not sure if this is a miniserve issue but it seems like reasonable behavior and it would be good to support this situation for compatibility.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nExpected:\n```\nsmall: 3 rows\nlarge: 1,000,000 rows\n```\n\nActual:\n```\nsmall: object-store error: Operation not supported: Range request not supported by  (path: http://127.0.0.1:34037/small.parquet)\nlarge: 1,000,000 rows\n```\n\n### Installed versions\n\n<details>\n\n```\n--------Version info---------\nPolars:              1.42.1\nIndex type:          UInt32\nPlatform:            Linux-5.14.0-570.58.1.el9_6.x86_64-x86_64-with-glibc2.34\nPython:              3.12.11 (main, Sep  2 2025, 14:20:58) [Clang 20.1.4 ]\nRuntime:             rt32\n\n----Optional dependencies----\nAzure CLI            <not installed>\nadbc_driver_manager  <not installed>\naltair               <not installed>\nazure.identity       <not installed>\nboto3                <not installed>\ncloudpickle          <not installed>\nconnectorx           <not installed>\ndeltalake            <not installed>\nfastexcel            <not installed>\nfsspec               <not installed>\ngevent               <not installed>\ngoogle.auth          <not installed>\ngreat_tables         <not installed>\nmatplotlib           <not installed>\nnumpy                <not 